====================================================================================
NEGATIVE TEST OF THE GATED STAGE 3 EXECUTION PATH
====================================================================================

  Subject   : harness/lib/run-joern-gated.sh, the only committed execution path for
              Stage 3, which runs harness/lib/preflight_graph_identity.py and reaches
              harness/bin/run-joern.sh only on a gate exit of 0.
  Question  : does a graph the write-time record does not describe actually stop the
              runner from being invoked -- not merely produce a warning beside it?
  Method    : alter ONE hex digit of the recorded digest, run the WRAPPER (not the
              gate alone), and measure whether the runner ran. The graph itself is
              never touched: what is perturbed is the record the graph is compared
              against, which is the only way to exercise the comparison without
              destroying 791,927,027 bytes and rebuilding them.
  Run at    : 2026-09-01T04:39:41Z
  Clone     : 0

  HOW 'THE RUNNER NEVER RAN' IS ESTABLISHED, rather than assumed:
    - harness/bin/run-joern.sh:64 runs 'rm -f $ART' BEFORE invoking Joern, and
      scope_finish rewrites joern.status at the end, so an invocation cannot leave
      the artifact, the console stream and the status file all byte-identical.
    - the wrapper prints a '== step 2/2' banner on the line immediately before it
      invokes the runner, so the count of that banner in its captured output is
      the count of invocations. Step 3 asserts that count is zero.
    - the real Stage 3 invocation of record took 1351 s (harness/artifacts/logs/
      joern.status elapsed_seconds); the refusal returns in seconds.

